                <pb facs="0558" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-10T14:00:00-05:00">February 10, 1933—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:19 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. Minister for Foreign Affairs called and asked me to emphasize second
                    paragraph of my 29, February 9, 9 p.m. (although I assured him Department
                    understood situation). He said he and the President were agreed acceptance
                    wording “in compensation” would mean revolution here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
